      "blocks": {
        "review_1": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image_asset": "pawsorb-review-1-toad.jpg",
            "focal": "50% 45%",
            "alt": "Woman by a Florida pool hugging her yellow Lab, holding a PawSorb tube",
            "name": "Dana R. · Tampa, FL",
            "tag": "Cane toad",
            "text": "<p>Moved to Tampa from Ohio two years ago. I honestly thought the big brown frogs around the pool were cute. Then in April our neighbor's dog licked one and was gone before they reached the ER. I ordered PawSorb that night. July, 10 p.m., I let Bo out for his last potty break and heard him gagging by the pool. Foam, pawing at his mouth, a toad sitting right there under the light. My hands were shaking. I wiped his gums with a wet rag, front to back. Bo is 78 pounds, so I gave him three tubes, squeezed into his cheek one after the other. Then I called the ER from the car. The vet said we did it right and that those first minutes mattered most. He was home by 2 a.m. and he's snoring on my feet as I type this. Keep enough for your dog's size by the back door. Please.</p>"
          }
        },
        "review_2": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image_asset": "pawsorb-review-2-chocolate.jpg",
            "focal": "50% 78%",
            "alt": "Beagle next to a torn chocolate wrapper on the kitchen floor",
            "name": "Megan T. · Columbus, OH",
            "tag": "Christmas chocolate",
            "text": "<p>Christmas Eve, 9 p.m. Our beagle Biscuit tore open a box of dark chocolates from under the tree. Our vet was closed till the 26th and the poison line had me on hold. So I dialed her to 22 pounds and gave the tube while I was still waiting. The ER checked her over and sent us home. We opened presents with her the next morning.</p>"
          }
        },
        "review_3": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image_asset": "pawsorb-review-3-small-dog.jpg",
            "focal": "55% 45%",
            "alt": "Man with his Shih Tzu, holding a PawSorb tube",
            "name": "Rick K. · Mesa, AZ",
            "tag": "Grapes",
            "text": "<p>Lulu is 9 pounds. Three grapes rolled off the counter and she beat me to them. I was shaking, but the dial did the math: 9 on the ring, squeeze, done. Thirty seconds. She's fine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "review_4": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image_asset": "pawsorb-review-4-trash.jpg",
            "focal": "50% 45%",
            "alt": "Golden retriever in a raided kitchen trash can",
            "name": "Jess M. · Knoxville, TN",
            "tag": "Rat bait",
            "text": "<p>My golden is a trash compactor, and this time he dragged a bait block out of the garage. Second scare this year. Gave him his tubes on the kitchen floor, then drove him in. Bloodwork came back clean. Bought three more for my parents, because he stays there every summer.</p>"
          }
        },
        "review_5": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image_asset": "pawsorb-review-5-holiday-pill.jpg",
            "focal": "50% 68%",
            "alt": "Dog under a holiday dinner table next to a dropped pill bottle",
            "name": "Sharon B. · Raleigh, NC",
            "tag": "Dropped pill",
            "text": "<p>Thanksgiving at my mom's. Dad dropped his heart pill and Penny had it before anyone reached under the table. I froze. My 15-year-old grabbed the PawSorb from my purse, read the steps printed on the tube and dialed her weight while I held her. Then we called the vet with the dose already in. Now there's a tube at Mom's, one at my sister's and one in my glovebox. Whoever is watching her can handle it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "review_6": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image_asset": "pawsorb-review-6-puppy.jpg",
            "focal": "60% 45%",
            "alt": "Man with a chocolate Lab puppy and a chewed chocolate bar wrapper",
            "name": "Tyler P. · Portland, OR",
            "tag": "Puppy + chocolate",
            "text": "<p>Our 11-week-old Lab pup chewed through half a dark chocolate bar I left on the couch. He weighed 14 pounds, so I dialed 14, gave it, then called the vet. Chasing his rope toy again by dinner. Should've been on our puppy list from day one.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
